From 62b6eb777b11588763772ca40793b03389c9cf9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:53:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 51/52] ppc32: pad the far jump slot's data tail to the 8 bytes
 the layout reserves

G5 parade #12 of the 12.4 port, the first wasm item.  turbofan-hot
passed in full; new WebAssembly.Module() died laying out the module's
far jump table:

  # Check failed: reinterpret_cast<Address>(pc_) & 0x7 == 0.
  ... JumpTableAssembler::SkipUntil + 0   (nearest symbol; the CHECK is
      EmitFarJumpSlot's alignment check)
  ... NativeModule::AddCodeSpaceLocked / NativeModule::NativeModule /
      WasmCodeManager::NewNativeModule

The ppc far slot is mov + LoadU64 + mtctr + bctr, nop-padded to
kFarJumpTableSlotSize - 8, then the CHECK, then dp(target) for the
8-byte data tail the mov points at and PatchFarJumpSlot rewrites.  dp()
emits a pointer-sized word - 4 bytes on ppc32 - so every slot came out
4 bytes short: the first slot's CHECK passes (the table base is
kCodeAlignment = 32-byte aligned), the second slot starts at +28 and
its CHECK fires at +52.  The ppc32 re-derivation of the constants
(kFarJumpTableSlotSize = 32, 0011-era) had sized the slot for the
8-byte tail but not noticed dp() shrinking it.

Emit a second, zero dp() on ppc32 after the pointer.  The slot is 32
bytes again; the pointer stays in the first word of the tail, which is
where LoadU64 (width-lowered to lwz by 0004) reads it and where
PatchFarJumpSlot's 4-byte atomic store at slot + 32 - 8 writes it, so
reader, writer and emitter agree.  Not a 64-bit word: on big-endian
that would put the 4-byte pointer in the high half, away from the lwz.

Checked alongside: the lazy-compile slot's two mov()s are at most
lis/ori pairs on ppc32 (kMovInstructionsNoConstantPool = 2; the jump
table assembler has no constant pool), so mov+mov+mtctr+bctr fits the
6-instruction slot; the near slot is the single relative b.  The far
table's own CHECK (used < size - 8) holds for the 4- or 5-instruction
sequence.
---
 v8/src/wasm/jump-table-assembler.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/wasm/jump-table-assembler.cc b/v8/src/wasm/jump-table-assembler.cc
index bbd43ce..3034140 100644
--- a/v8/src/wasm/jump-table-assembler.cc
+++ b/v8/src/wasm/jump-table-assembler.cc
@@ -481,6 +481,14 @@ void JumpTableAssembler::EmitFarJumpSlot(Address target) {
   NopBytes(kFarJumpTableSlotSize - 8 - used);
   CHECK_EQ(reinterpret_cast<Address>(pc_) & 0x7, 0);  // Alignment
   dp(target);
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC
+  // dp() emits a pointer-sized word, 4 bytes here, while the slot reserves
+  // (and PatchFarJumpSlot addresses) an 8-byte tail; pad so the slot keeps
+  // its full kFarJumpTableSlotSize and the next slot's alignment.  The
+  // pointer stays in the first word, where LoadU64 (lwz) and the patch
+  // store read and write it.
+  dp(0);
+#endif
 }
 
 // static
